<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maumoon Abdul Gayoom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maumoon Abdul Gayoom was president of the Maldives from 1978 to 2008, the longest-serving leader in the country's history. His government developed tourism and fisheries and survived a coup attempt by Sri Lankan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> in 1988, defeated with Indian help, but restricted political opposition. He lost the first multi-party election in 2008 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-nasheed">Mohamed Nasheed</a>.</p></div>
